=== C. BBT extras and curvature ===
C1. #1 s6: 3H^2 (M_P^2 + Mt^2 a^-6) = rho; the factor is positive for all a > 0: True -> H = 0 iff rho = 0
C2. dictionary (#1 s6): rho_eff = E/a^3, E = rhotilde*atilde^3, atilde = 1/a  ->  rho_eff = rhotilde/a**6 (sign of rhotilde preserved)
C3. negative dark radiation (closed dual curvature), exaggerated to Omega_dr = -1e-3, written form c = 1:
flat+dr: c=1.0, f=1.0, tau_i/f=0.5: V0=1.1383, min V = V0(c-1) = 0.0000; today H=1.0000, Omega_tau=0.7010, w0=-0.9877
    no turnaround up to t = 2000/H0: a = 2161, min H after today = 0.0003339, H*t = 0.6677 (dust-like value 2/3 = 0.6667), V(tau) at end = 6.587e-09, R = 3H^2 = 3.344e-07
C4. NOT in the documents (their Friedmann equation, #1 s6, has no curvature term): closed OUR-frame
    space with the written form c = 1. Omega_k0 = -0.1 is excluded by data; it is used only so the
    recollapse falls inside the integration window. It shows the mechanism, not a viable model.
